    {
      "id": "claim_80c165723d094986bff45bde70e5e214",
      "statement": "The answer-code wire format is sdpEncode(localAnswerSdp) + '|' + publicKeyBase64 (key empty when the receiver downgraded to plaintext — a valid, intentional artifact); the offer peer's parseAnswerCode splits on the LAST '|', distinguishes a missing separator from a well-formed empty-key code (which follows the receiver into plaintext via effectiveEncrypt=false instead of dead-ending the handshake), imports a non-empty RSA public key inside a try/catch that toasts 'Invalid encryption key in answer code' and aborts on failure, and applies the decoded answer via setRemoteDescription inside its own try/catch that toasts 'Invalid answer code' on malformed SDP (PR #45); the receive page likewise decodes the user-controllable s param and calls setRemoteDescription inside a try/catch that toasts 'Invalid SDP in link' instead of crashing the page during load (PR #45).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/OfferPage.svelte#L276-L333",
