    {
      "id": "claim_45433c561b6d45cd86f0cfa35e29ca90",
      "statement": "Both sides wait for ICE candidates to drain before freezing the SDP into the shareable artifact, but a 3-second WAIT_ICE_CANDIDATES_TIMEOUT builds the link/answer code from the current localDescription anyway so the connection forms rather than hanging; on the offer side the RSA keypair is minted once at the top of generateOfferLink and a per-invocation offerBuilt flag claims the build synchronously so the two paths build the link at most once, and the whole generation is try/catch-guarded so a construction/offer failure toasts 'Could not generate the offer' instead of leaving the spinner stuck. Regeneration is generation-safe: before minting, the pending ICE-candidate timer is cleared, the old data channel's handlers are nulled and it is closed, the old RTCPeerConnection is closed (guarded on connectionState !== 'closed' since close() throws InvalidStateError on an already-settled peer), the settled peer crypto is reset (rsaPub = undefined, effectiveEncrypt re-pinned from the live setting, so the new generation never encrypts with the previous peer's RSA key — PR #68) and the dead generation's UI state (new-file badge, isConnecting, pending answer code) is cleared, and a monotonically increasing offerGeneration counter is bumped; the timeout fallback re-checks its captured generation at fire time so a stale timer holding the previous generation's public key can never build a link with the old key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/OfferPage.svelte#L153-L284",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4440415b20d38fefa38d520881db38583f90f483f2f95948e0ca7c2cf171b038:"
