    {
      "id": "claim_a18f75c58d0648e6b3879e26bff57b82",
      "statement": "Failure handling: a missing or empty 's' param on the receive page redirects to origin and throws; ICE candidate errors, data channel errors, and close events toast an error, clear isConnecting, and blank the offer link on the offer side to prevent reuse of a stale link; onerror and onclose additionally call sender?.onChannelClose()/receiver?.onChannelClose() so in-flight/queued files on both sides exit with an accurate 'connection lost' error instead of dead-ending or re-firing false per-chunk errors (PR #74); offer-generation failures (synchronous constructor throws or rejected createOffer/setLocalDescription) toast 'Could not generate the offer' and re-enable the button; and on the receive side an unappliable offer sets offerFailed, which replaces the perpetual 'Generating Answer' spinner with an error state ('Could not connect: the offer in the link is invalid') instead of dead-ending the page (PR #49).",
